# 5. I therefore recommend a state-aware entity interpretation layer

Instead of assuming:

```text
NER → final semantic meaning
```

we should do:

```text
                    ┌── Intent classifier
User message ───────┤
                    └── NER
                         ↓
                  State-aware interpreter
                         ↓
                    State machine
```

For example:

### Initial request

```text
User:
بدي تكسي من ساحة البريد لحي المعلمين
```

NER:

```text
ساحة البريد       PICKUP
حي المعلمين       DEST
```

No ambiguity.

---

### Follow-up for pickup

```text
State:
waiting_for_pickup

User:
ساحة البريد
```

NER:

```text
ساحة البريد → location-like entity
```

State says:

```text
waiting_for_pickup
        ↓
interpret location as PICKUP
```

---

### Follow-up for destination

```text
State:
waiting_for_dest

User:
ساحة البريد
```

Same NER output.

But:

```text
waiting_for_dest
        ↓
interpret location as DEST
```

This is much more robust.

